    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0940" n="838" xml:id="pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1529: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-03T14:00:00+01:00">October 3, 1935—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 3—12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>412. Consulate’s 408 October 2, 5 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d712-f1"/> A member
                    of the Council stated to me today that “some consideration” was being given to
                    soliciting the participation of the American Government in possible operations
                    by airplane of “impartial observers”. In fact I was asked concerning the nearest
                    posts where American military attachés were stationed. General reference was
                    made in this connection to our participation in the Manchurian inquiry.</p>
                <p>While I am at present disinclined to think that there is anything in this I am
                    reporting what was said to me.</p>
                <p>I feel it would be useful in a general sense to have as background the
                    Department’s comments. Please instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
